.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Wake-word training artifacts. ~19GB: a 17GB precomputed negative-feature
# dump, ~40k synthesised WAV clips, a second venv with CPU torch in it, and
# the cloned sample generator. All of it is either downloadable or
# regenerable by training/run.sh, and none of it belongs in git -- committing
# the feature dump alone would make every future clone of this repo pay 17GB.
#
# The trained models themselves are NOT ignored: they live in
# src/friday/models/*.onnx, are ~850KB each, and are the one artifact that
# must ship with the code that loads them.
training/.venv-train/
training/piper-sample-generator/
training/data/
training/clips/
training/features/
training/models/
training/*.log

# microWakeWord has an isolated environment and potentially very large,
# licensed datasets. Keep manifests/config/results; never commit raw corpora,
# generated features, local recordings, or virtual environments.
tools/microwakeword/.venv/
tools/microwakeword/.venv-piper/
tools/microwakeword/vendor/
tools/microwakeword/datasets/raw/
tools/microwakeword/datasets/downloads/
tools/microwakeword/datasets/features/
tools/microwakeword/datasets/generated/
tools/microwakeword/datasets/ambient/
tools/microwakeword/artifacts/*/checkpoints/
tools/microwakeword/artifacts/*/saved_models/
tools/microwakeword/artifacts/*/runtime-config.yaml
tools/microwakeword/artifacts/*/work/

# Local working notes -- deliberately not published (see git history: a
# previous HANDOUT.md was folded into README.md in 4b95490).
HANDOUT.md
